{"ticker":"MOIL","symbol":"MOIL","instrumentId":3116012,"name":"Moil","industry":"NSE-Mining-Metal Ores","about":"MOIL Ltd. is the largest manganese ore producer in India, with 11 mines located across Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh. The company plays a crucial role in the steel manufacturing sector, supplying high-grade manganese ore used in steelmaking and alloy production. MOIL’s operations include mining, beneficiation, and the production of ferroalloys, enhancing the quality and usability of the extracted ore. With a strong focus on sustainable mining practices, MOIL is committed to efficient resource management and minimizing environmental impact. The company also invests in R&D to optimize production processes, reinforcing its position as a key player in India's manganese market.","website":"www.moil.nic.in","location":"NAGPUR, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:42:04.969Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":213.86,"changePct":1.2642644064586466,"week52High":380.55,"week52Low":203.22},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹4,352 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹740 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"71,219,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"78"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"16,545,771"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"2.68%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"1.61"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.7"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.15"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.1"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"3%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"22.12"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"9–34"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"9.9%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"7.73"},{"label":"Volume","value":"322,291"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"508,620"},{"label":"Master score","value":"39"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"49"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"15"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"160"},{"label":"Acc/Dis rating","value":"C"}],"earningsAnnual":{"hea